From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmstyle: command, chord, mute, style, motif and audition tracks keep and answer their data; style time signature and tempo; DirectMusicSection object

The dmstyle tracks were stubs returning S_OK. They now:
- keep what they load or are given: command track ('cmnd'), chord track ('cord' list), mute track ('mute'), style track (style
  references, SetParam), and answer GetParam/SetParam (CommandParam, CommandParam2, CommandParamNext, ChordParam, RhythmParam,
  MuteParam, IDirectMusicStyle, TimeSignature, Disable/EnableTimeSig, SeedVariations) with the documented structures and
  DMUS_E_NOT_FOUND / DMUS_E_TYPE_DISABLED / DMUS_E_*_UNSUPPORTED answers;
- Init/InitPlay/EndPlay validate their arguments (E_POINTER) and keep a play state for GetParamEx/SetParamEx; PlayEx,
  GetParamEx and SetParamEx convert reference times through the performance; Clone ([start,end) moved to zero, the item in effect
  at start carried), Join (same class only), Save for the command, chord and mute tracks;
- command and chord tracks send notification messages when GUID_NOTIFICATION_COMMAND / _CHORD was added; other tracks answer
  S_FALSE to AddNotificationType (mute track stays E_NOTIMPL);
- style: GetTimeSignature and GetTempo return the style header (defaults 4/4, 120);
- DirectMusicSection can be created (IDirectMusicObject + IPersistStream, Load E_NOTIMPL).
Pattern playback (Play of the style, motif and audition tracks) is not implemented and still logs a FIXME. The todo_wine marks
of the tests which pass are removed.
